The Eastern Orthodox calendar therefore places his feast on April 2, shared with Aedisius, whom some call his brother.'::text) || jsonb_build_object('provenance', '{"article": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amphian", "biography": "rewritten"}'::jsonb),
